  "notes": "Primary school is an eight-year cycle: Junior and Senior Infants, then First to Sixth Class. All eight are listed, from age 5, although school is compulsory only from 6. Transition Year, an optional year between Third and Fifth Year taken by most students, is not a level: students who skip it go straight to Fifth Year."
